 Companion docs: `docs/ROADMAP.md` holds the *work* (pilot freeze items H1–H6, known issues/residuals); `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` holds the *capability census*; `docs/SOUND_PRODUCTION_SPEC.md` holds the sound-asset *production procedure*. This file holds *decisions*. (Consolidated from the former `PILOT_READINESS.md`, 2026-06-20.)
 
-**Study design (locked 2026-05-29).** Three-arm between-subjects pilot: phoneme sonification / engagement-matched arbitrary-sound / silent control. N≈40 kindergarten/Vorschule. Single session 10–20 min. Sound-off post-test. Framed as a pilot throughout.
+**Study design (locked 2026-05-29; third arm redesigned 2026-07-06).** Three-arm between-subjects pilot: phoneme / **spatial 2D sonification** / silent control. N≈40 kindergarten/Vorschule. Single session 10–20 min. Study letter set A F I L M (uppercase), each child trains a counterbalanced 3-of-5 subset. Sound-off post-test (designed, not yet built). Framed as a pilot throughout.
+
+> **Supersession notice (ledger brought into line with code, 2026-09-01; David's sign-off pending).** Commits `9a52c9a` and `b641022` (2026-07-06) implemented a redesign that this ledger had not yet recorded:
+> - **D2 is SUPERSEDED.** The third arm is no longer an engagement-matched abstract sound per letter. It is a spatial sonification: one shared, letter-independent carrier (seamless band-limited 440 Hz triangle, `Resources/Sonification/spatial_carrier.wav`) whose **pitch follows pen Y** (220–880 Hz, linear in cents, top = high) and whose pan follows pen X. No per-letter abstract sounds are needed; the Groß-Vogt abstract-sound design ask is off the critical path (ROADMAP H4 superseded).
+> - **D7 condition (1) NO LONGER HOLDS.** Pitch is driven **only in the spatial arm** (`setSpatialPitch`, per tick); the phoneme arm never drives pitch (regression test "phoneme arm: a touch never drives pitch"). The two sound arms are therefore matched on rate + pan + activation rules + headphone delivery, and **differ in two dimensions: sound identity (letter-specific phoneme vs letter-independent carrier) and pitch drive.** The §2.6 "matched on every property" discipline is replaced by an explicit statement of what is and is not matched (thesis Ch.4 §4.6, Ch.6 §6.5): the phoneme–spatial contrast compares two kinds of auditory content and is exploratory; the primary contrast is phoneme vs silent.
+> - **D6 is MOOT for the pilot set.** A F I L M are all vowels/continuants; the stop-consonant looping question is deferred to the full alphabet.
+> - **D9 (new, 2026-07-06): study letter set = A F I L M uppercase; practice pool = trained 3 of 5 (10 counterbalanced subsets from UUID byte 8); H6 post-test covers all 5, untrained pair = within-child comparison (not an inert baseline — Labat et al. 2015 found gains on untrained letters).**
+> - **D10 (new, 2026-07-06): clean study configuration under `studyMode`** — null speech/prompt/haptics in every arm, no celebration/reward overlays, difficulty pinned, retry gate off, fixed letter order, Druckschrift pinned. Outside `studyMode` behaviour is unchanged.
+> - **Protocol precondition (not code):** `thesisCondition` is NOT pinned by `studyMode`; the researcher override must be set to the full four-phase flow on every study device, because `guidedOnly`/`control` omit freeWrite and yield no Fréchet outcome.
+> - The rationale sections below for D2 and D7 are retained as history and no longer describe the shipped design.
+
 
 **Governance (David, 2026-05-30).**
 - No in-app consent / minor-assent UX required; KUG ethics does not require committee approval for this pilot. → consent UX is NOT a freeze item.
